@@s001 Code: edit distance in Java
@@s002 Code: edit distance in Java
@@s003 The edit distance in Java: the table of prefixes, the base cases, and the minimum of the three neighbours.
@@s004 Base cases and filling
@@s005 The table <code>opt[i][j]</code> is the distance between the first i characters of <code>a</code> and the first j of <code>b</code>.
@@s006 Base cases and filling
@@s007 Table of (n+1)×(m+1) cells: one extra row and one extra column for the empty case.
@@s008 Base case: I delete all the characters of a.
@@s009 If the two characters are equal the cost is 0, otherwise 1 (substitution).
@@s010 The minimum of the three neighbours: deletion, insertion, alignment.
@@s011 Syntax notes
@@s012 <code>a.charAt(i - 1)</code> gives the character at position <code>i − 1</code>: strings are indexed from zero.
@@s013 The ternary operator <code>(cond) ? x : y</code> is an <code>if</code> on one line.
